this is for the 164sx (samsung, 533mhz)


1.) prepare 2 floppy disks.
    format them on a DOS-PC (normal FAT)

2.) go to 
http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/v5.4/alphapc164sx/
   download 

fwupdate.exe 
sx164_v5_4.sys 

3.) put fwupdate.exe on the first DOS Floppy
    put sx164_v5_4.sys on the second DOS Floppy


4.) power off the alpha and open the case of your alpha

5.) set the "last" jumper to the "other" position.
    (the docu calls the jumper emergency something ....)

6.) put disk1 with fwupdate.exe in the floppy, 
    start the alpha

7.) insert disk2 with the sx164_v5_4.sys file when
    the system asks for additional disks

8.) in the UPD >> 
    do a:
    update fw -path fw_srm
    (this loads the srm firmware)

9.) ignore messages about not having found fw_nt.
    (at least my box has not enough onboard ram to hold
    alphabios and srm at the same time)

10.) exit the UPD, power off the machine. bring back
    the jumper on the motherboard in it's old position.

11.) reboot - your should be in the srm console now.


