On 2000-Apr-12 04:36:55 +1000, Jim King <king@sstar.com> wrote:
>You can try netbooting.  I've heard that this works. :-)

FreeBSD's netboot is not compatible with the latest SRM (3.8.3).  It
fits midway between the `old' and `new' boot styles and needs a patch
to /usr/src/sys/boot/alpha/libalpha/srmnet.c 1.4 to make it work.

